   244	## 7. Per-turn latency budget and measurement plan
   245	
   246	**Budget (design targets from F1, not measurements):**
   247	
   248	- turn 0 (import, load, warm-up, first act) ≤ 20 s, leaving ≥ 40 s of the bank;
   249	- steady-state p99 ≤ 500 ms and max < 900 ms;
   250	- the sum of per-turn excess over 1 s stays ≤ 10 s for a full episode.
   251	
   252	**Arithmetic estimate (unmeasured).**
   253	
   254	- The CPU path runs the padded trunk: 699 entity tokens + 2 player + 1 global +
   255	  4 scratch + 1 plan + 2 critic = **709 tokens**.
   256	- Linear FLOPs are about 2 × 4.22M trunk params × 709 ≈ 6.0 GFLOP.
   257	- Attention is about 8 layers × 4 × 709² × 256 ≈ 4.1 GFLOP.
   258	- That is ≈ 10 GFLOP per row. At an assumed 20–60 GFLOP/s single-thread fp32
   259	  it takes ≈ 170–500 ms.
   260	- The grammar heads run 7 unit slots batched over actors, then ≤ 10 market
   261	  positions: many small kernels whose cost is dispatch-bound, not
