ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:107:| `V3_IMPORT.json` | 1 | Manifest of the full prior import; new trim manifest supersedes it for this package |
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:126:**Decision proposed for Claude:** do not create a shared workspace or a root path dependency in Task 1.1. The root `Cargo.toml` has no `[workspace]`, no engine dependency, and root `src/` has no engine consumer. A nested independent Cargo package needs neither a root workspace entry nor a root dependency. Its own lockfile and explicit `--manifest-path` commands give a separate feature resolution. Keep root manifest/lock/source byte-identical.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:128:Task 1.2 lives inside the engine package. Task 1.3's planned `src/kaggriculture/observe.rs` may become the first root consumer when compiled against `Game`; Task 1.4 certainly will. Add the path dependency at the **first actual compiled consumer**, after reviewing that task, rather than claiming nothing before 1.4 can need it. There is no consumer that justifies it in **this** task.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:130:Workspace membership is not a dependency edge, but it is also **not feature isolation**. Cargo's locally installed primary documentation (`share/doc/rust/html/cargo/reference/resolver.html`, “Features”, in `nightly-2026-04-18-aarch64-apple-darwin`) explicitly states that selecting multiple workspace packages with `--workspace` or multiple `-p` flags unifies dependency features; separate invocations avoid that unification. A shared workspace also shares lock resolution. Resolver 2/3 does not isolate a normal engine dependency from the root's active test dependency on the same `serde_json` package. A root-only default invocation can avoid the engine when no dependency selects it, but `cargo test --workspace` would reintroduce L4.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:132:Keep engine `serde_json` features `arbitrary_precision` and `preserve_order`: removing them breaks the kernel's tested unbounded integer/numeric and ordered-inventory semantics. If Claude chooses a shared workspace now, the minimal way to keep unmodified root decoding is **separate package test invocations** (never selecting both); the more robust choice is the standalone package proposed here. Once the root needs the path dependency, apply the reference's narrow test-only repair, not feature deletion:
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:158:- All **25 registry packages** in the reference engine lockfile are present in the local Cargo cache. A temporary copy of its unchanged `Cargo.toml`/`Cargo.lock` passed `cargo metadata --offline --locked --format-version 1` (26 packages including the engine). No missing engine crates, downloads, or engine compilation. Metadata resolution is not proof of compilation.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:183:Expected: `kg/rebuild-codex`, the pinned reference commit, root **155 passed / 2 ignored**, no `serde_json` arbitrary-precision feature. `gzip` is installed. Preserve unrelated dirty work; if fixtures/cache are missing report the exact path/package instead of downloading or disabling parity.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:257:The sections above describe historical full imports, not this trimmed package.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:271:for the reviewed import plan. The root crate does not yet depend on this package.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:334:- [ ] **Step 1: Add a Kaggriculture section to the parity doc.** State the package pin, Python engine target, seven deletions, 41 retained unit tests, 9 RNG tests, four trace IDs/seeds/banks and 2,876 transitions / 2,880 snapshots. Identify all new harness tests separately, the 79+1 excluded tests and why, private-order/numeric comparisons, standalone dependency boundary and L4 reopening condition. Mark outcome pending until commands below finish; preserve existing Orbit coverage.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:349:Expected root result on every invocation: **155 passed / 2 ignored**, unchanged fixture coverage. `just rs-prepare` and `just prepare` cover the **root package only**; the explicit engine test and manifest invocations above are additional mandatory checks, not implicitly covered by `just`. Root formatting must not traverse the standalone engine. The baseline full Python suite is 722 passed / 3 platform skips; no Python implementation changes are planned. Use real exit codes when saving logs (no pipeline masking). No further repeat is needed after a successful final check unless code changes.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:565:Expected **12 Node tests**. They exercise genuine drift and inventory failures with tiny buffers; they neither copy nor compile the full engine. End-to-end `check()` is then run on the actual package at every acceptance gate.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:774:**Claude to confirm:** use the standalone package for Task 1.1 instead of the parent plan's shared workspace, and defer `fixture_float` to the first root dependency integration. The new replay test is required to make the four retained traces active parity evidence. This is implementation review, not a request for an owner recipe decision.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:7:**Architecture:** Put the production module in `src/kaggriculture/grammar.rs`, compiled by the root crate through `src/kaggriculture.rs`. An authored integration test in the standalone engine package includes that **same source file** by path and calls `Game::step`; it does not link the root crate into the engine. Export a small validated plan/cursor and factored boolean tables instead of the reference binary DFA. No root → engine dependency is added in 1.2; L4 reopens at the first production engine consumer in 1.3/1.4.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:27:| `src/kaggriculture/grammar_tests.rs` | Codex / authored, create | Module tests: supports, reachable states, quantities, HIRE law, recorded oracle and transport errors. Include from `grammar.rs` with `#[cfg(test)] #[path = "grammar_tests.rs"] mod tests;`; use only `super` and package-common dependencies so both packages can compile it. |
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:49:The pinned `lib.rs` has exactly seven declaration removals, including `myolie_sampler`; adding `mod grammar` violates `W:scripts/check_engine_trim.py:384–394`. The engine manifest and lockfile also have exact derived contents (`:395–408`), and the checker presently accepts only one authored path (`:234–239`). Merely creating `engine_rs/src/grammar.rs` would provide neither compilation nor permission to declare it. Use the normal root module tree, consistent with `W:src/rl.rs:1–3`, and a narrow test-only path include for the engine integration. This compiles one implementation in two separate Cargo invocations, against each package's existing Serde JSON configuration; it does not copy a second grammar or require root `rlib` output (`W:Cargo.toml:6–9`).
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:51:Only the new engine test needs an `authored` entry. Root files belong in `non_engine_changes`, not in `retained`. Update `verify_task_authored`'s explicit expected list and its error label; do not accept arbitrary paths declared by the manifest. Add negative checks for a third self-declared source, a missing test and an incorrect authored hash. The existing exact retained set, LICENSE protection and appendix hash remain in force (`W:scripts/check_engine_trim.py:15–42,270–312,354–412`). No change to `engine_rs/VENDORED_FROM.md` is needed; its Task 1.1 statement that the root does not depend on the package remains true (`:57–73`).
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:303:The shared test module resolves fixture paths explicitly by package: `CARGO_PKG_NAME == "owl"` uses `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`; `"kaggriculture-engine"` uses its parent. Reject any other package name. Join `tests/fixtures/kaggriculture/grammar-v4-reference.jsonl.gz` to that root. Never search arbitrary fallback paths; the same test source runs in both packages.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:307:Question: is the proposed path actually compiled without changing the pinned package? Inputs: root registry and standalone engine checker. Stop when module constants compile and the exact two-path authored inventory passes.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:317:There is no existing grammar recorder identified in the inspected reference paths. Author the recorder/harness listed in §1. **Do not generate expected results with the new grammar.** The driver loads `actor_codec.py` from the scratch reference by explicit file path for replay encoding, loads the reference binary plans returned by the harness with `struct`, and uses only these sources to form expectations. Do not import the package `owl`/Torch or require the reference PyO3 extension.
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:564:- [ ] `grammar.rs` is self-contained and passes both packages' Clippy; the retirement condition for the engine-test include is recorded for 1.3/1.4 (R2).
ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.2.md:574:- **L4 / feature graph:** a normal production root → engine edge unifies `serde_json/arbitrary_precision` and may break the test-only internally tagged float decode. Separate-package tests do not qualify that future graph. Keep numeric features, reopen with the narrow fixture repair and generation tests at the actual dependency addition. Evidence: `W:ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/1.1-rules-kernel.md:124–153`; `W:src/rules_engine/generation.rs:691–697`.
